--TEST--
`Core\Config::setting` gives `null` for a name no block sets, so `as int` throws, and `as ?int` gives `null` — `rule:config/settings-and-secrets-are-a-programs-own-values`
--FILE nvs.toml--
[settings]
page_size = "ten"
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `as ?int` gives `null` for a missing value.
echo Core\Json::encode(Core\Config::setting('missing') as ?int), "\n";

// `missing` is not set, so `as int` throws an error and the program stops.
echo Core\Config::setting('missing') as int, "\n";
echo "not reached\n";
--EXPECT--
null
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
%s"msg":"cannot convert this value to `int`"%s"line":6%s
